# M3-W1 native UI workaround attempt — branch fired, app crashed in LauncherProfilesViewController (splitViewController nil)
# date: 2026-11-01T08:51:12-1000

Attempt: native build marker VRMCNativeBuild=true in Info.plist; launchInitialViewController swaps root from LauncherSplitViewController to LauncherNavigationController(root=LauncherProfilesViewController).
Evidence: native-ui.log 'rootVC=<LauncherNavigationController>' and latestlog '[VRMC-NATIVE] rootVC=LauncherNavigationController (visionOS native workaround)' => the native branch executed.

Result: app crashes with NSException. lastExceptionBacktrace: __exceptionPreprocess -> objc_exception_throw -> -[__NSPlaceholderArray initWithObjects:count:] -> -[LauncherProfilesViewController viewWillAppear:].
Cause: LauncherMenuViewController.h defines sidebarNavController/sidebarViewController via self.splitViewController.viewControllers[0]; with a plain LauncherNavigationController root, splitViewController is nil, so the array literal @[sidebarViewController drawAccountButton, self.createButtonItem] receives nil and throws.

Conclusion: the native launcher cannot be fixed by merely swapping the root view controller; the UIKit launcher VCs hard-assume a UISplitViewController. M3-W1 needs a native-specific UI shell (or a split-view-compatible shim) that can invoke the existing launch path. Auto-launch remains the only working boot path (EV-0077).

Per operator instruction, export/ was cleared of the old Amethyst/LWJGL issue and replaced with this native-UI blocker dossier. Compat launcher restored.
